  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "If three times the larger of two numbers is four times the smaller and the difference between the numbers is \\(8,\\) then the larger of the two numbers is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(16\\)",
    "B": "\\(24\\)",
    "C": "\\(32\\)",
    "D": "\\(44\\)",
    "E": "\\(52\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Let \\(L\\) be the larger number. Since the difference is \\(8\\), the smaller number is \\(L-8\\). This lets us express both numbers with one unknown. The multiple condition becomes\n\\[\n3L=4(L-8)=4L-32.\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(3L\\) and then adding \\(32\\) gives \\(L=32\\). The smaller number is \\(24\\), and\n\\[\n32-24=8,\\qquad3\\cdot32=4\\cdot24=96.\n\\]\nThus the larger number is \\(32\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
